\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\section{Background}
Program synthesis has a long history in the programming languages community.
\subsection{Prior Work}
Early systems studied the problem first from a deductive perspective, deriving programs from specifications.
\subsection{Prior Work (Cont.)}
Later approaches approach it differently, searching large candidate spaces with statistical guidance.
\section{Our Approach}
We combine both views.
\end{document}

